 150","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":312.6625,"dec":60.3,"maj":60.0,"notes":"Curved dark marking; 1 degree long","con":"Cep","s":"B 150 | Barnard 150"},{"id":"B151","n":"B 151","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":317.0542,"dec":56.3167,"maj":60.0,"notes":"Very small; very dark; diam. 1 degree; about 14' N of BD +55 2529 (magnitude 7.5); apparently a real object in a slightly larger vacancy","con":"Cep","s":"B 151 | Barnard 151"},{"id":"B152","n":"B 152","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":318.6208,"dec":61.7333,"maj":9.0,"notes":"Small; 15'x3' SE and NW","con":"Cep","s":"B 152 | Barnard 152"},{"id":"B153","n":"B 153","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":320.2625,"dec":56.4333,"maj":60.0,"notes":"Black; irregular; diam. 1 degree; 5' S of BD +55 2565 (magnitude 7.4)","con":"Cep","s":"B 153 | Barnard 153"},{"id":"B154","n":"B 154","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":320.3417,"dec":56.6,"maj":8.0,"notes":"Narrow; 8' long NE and SW; BD +55 2565 (magnitude 7.4) at the S end","con":"Cep","s":"B 154 | Barnard 154"},{"id":"B155","n":"B 155","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":323.0333,"dec":44.9667,"maj":13.0,"notes":"Round; diam. 13'; indefinite; four small stars in a line crossing it E and W","con":"Cyg","s":"B 155 | Barnard 155"},{"id":"B156","n":"B 156","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":323.4958,"dec":45.5833,"maj":8.0,"notes":"Diam. 8'; sharp pointed to N; BD +44 3865 (magnitude 4.1) in center","con":"Cyg","s":"B 156 | Barnard 156"},{"id":"B157","n":"B 157","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":323.4208,"dec":54.6667,"maj":5.0,"notes":"Round; diam. 5'; 8' plus or minus W of BD +54 2576 (magnitude 8.3); a semicircle of faint stars forms the western border","con":"Cyg","s":"B 157 | Barnard 157"},{"id":"B158","n":"B 158","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":324.3042,"dec":43.4,"maj":3.0,"notes":"Dark spot; diam. 3'; similar to those in the region of B 159. There are some others N and W of this","con":"Cyg","s":"B 158 | Barnard 158"},{"id":"B159","n":"B 159","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":324.5917,"dec":43.2167,"maj":25.0,"notes":"Irregular partially vacant region; diam. 25'","con":"Cyg","s":"B 159 | Barnard 159"},{"id":"B160","n":"B 160","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":324.4917,"dec":56.2167,"maj":31.0,"notes":"Large, dark; irregular; diam. 31' NE and SW","con":"Cep","s":"B 160 | Barnard 160"},{"id":"B161","n":"B 161","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":325.0917,"dec":57.8167,"maj":3.0,"notes":"Small, black spot. This is one of the comet-shaped objects. The head is very sharp and black, 3' across. This extends north for some 3', then widens out into a less dense tail about 13' long.","con":"Cep","s":"B 161 | Barnard 161"},{"id":"B162","n":"B 162","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":325.2875,"dec":56.3167,"maj":13.0,"notes":"Very thin, curved dark strip, 13' N and S; a curve of small stars on the SW end","con":"Cep","s":"B 162 | Barnard 162"},{"id":"B163","n":"B 163","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":325.5417,"dec":56.7,"notes":"Small; very black; pointed to the S; two dark streams running from this to the N","con":"Cep","s":"B 163 | Barnard 163"},{"id":"B164","n":"B 164","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":326.6292,"dec":51.0833,"maj":20.0,"notes":"V-shaped vacancy; 20' N and S","con":"Cyg","s":"B 164 | Barnard 164"},{"id":"B165","n":"B 165","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":327.2333,"dec":60.2,"maj":18.0,"notes":"Length E and W 18', width 1'; BD +59 2424 (magnitude 7.8) near the E end","con":"Cep","s":"B 165 | Barnard 165"},{"id":"B166","n":"B 166","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":327.7708,"dec":60.0833,"maj":5.0,"notes":"Round; diam 5'; small star on SW edge","con":"Cep","s":"B 166 | Barnard 166"},{"id":"B167","n":"B 167","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":327.9917,"dec":60.0667,"maj":5.0,"notes":"Small; irregularly round; diam 5'; about 7' N of BD +59 2427 (magnitude 7.7)","con":"Cep","s":"B 167 | Barnard 167"},{"id":"B168","n":"B 168","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":328.3333,"dec":47.2667,"maj":10.0,"notes":"Small nebula at E end of dark lane. This nebula is 10' in diameter with over a dozen stars of different magnitudes in it. There is no central condensation, nor does the nebula condense about any of the stars. There are some dark markings in it. The dark lane is 1.7 degrees long and 9' wide (see Lick","con":"Cyg","s":"B 168 | Barnard 168"},{"id":"B169","n":"B 169","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":329.7167,"dec":58.75,"maj":60.0,"notes":"Elliptical black ring; diam. 1 degree. This incloses an \"island\" of small stars. The dark ring is broadest on its east side where its thickness is 22'. The northern part is very black and straight. BD +58 2371 (magnitude 8.5) is in the northeast part of the \"island\" of stars.","con":"Cep","s":"B 169 | Barnard 169"},{"id":"B170","n":"B 170","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":329.5083,"dec":58.95,"maj":15.0,"notes":"Irregular black strip 26' long NE and SW, 4' wide. This is the northwest border of the island of small stars. It is sharply defined and darker than the sky.","con":"Cep","s":"B 170 | Barnard 170"},{"id":"B171","n":"B 171","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":330.325,"dec":58.8667,"maj":91.0,"notes":"Irregular, broken region; diam. 19'; at the E end of the \"island\" of small stars","con":"Cep","s":"B 171 | Barnard 171"},{"id":"B173","n":"B 173","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":331.8667,"dec":59.6667,"maj":4.0,"notes":"Diam. 4'; rather definite; a small star on N edge and one on SW edge","con":"Cep","s":"B 173 | Barnard 173"},{"id":"B174","n":"B 174","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":331.8292,"dec":59.0667,"maj":19.0,"notes":"Narrow; irregular; 19' long NE and SW","con":"Cep","s":"B 174 | Barnard 174"},{"id":"B175","n":"B 175","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":333.5,"dec":69.9333,"maj":60.0,"notes":"Large; diam. 1 degree; bright nebula in N part. This is a large dark spot, extended north and south, 62' in its largest diameter. In its upper part is the star BD +69 1231 (magnitude 8.8), which is nebulous. This is apparently a large dark nebula, the brighter part of which forms the star +69 1231. ","con":"Cep","s":"B 175 | Barnard 175"},{"id":"B201","n":"B 201","src":"B","t":"DrkN","ra":33.25,"dec":57.0833,"maj":10.0,"notes":"Small; diam. 10'; 45' W of NGC 